          "A daily report of 400 CVEs with no triage is read by nobody: the team turns the scanner off. You need: severity in your context (is the code even called), whether an exploit exists, whether a fix exists, and an SLO for the fix (critical — days, low — the next cycle). An ignore has a reason and a review date, not 'forever'. Scan the lock file and the final image (including OS packages of the base layer), not only package.json. A transitive dependency update is checked with tests. Do not confuse 'a GPL license in an internal client' with a CVE — that is a different process, also from the SBOM.",
