          "Sometimes a policy gets in the way of fixing an incident: you need a deliberate bypass (break-glass) — a short-lived role, a limited time, a mandatory 'why' record, and a notice to the security channel. That is not a permanent exception in the policy code 'for this service forever'. After the window, rights are revoked automatically, and the session is reviewed. A bypass with no journal is a hole you cannot tell from an attack. Rehearse the procedure in a tabletop: who approves, how long, what is logged. Do not leave a permanent cluster-admin kubeconfig in a shared folder 'just in case' — that is not break-glass, it is a leak.",
